-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787855413660243001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"3bee96c3-23b6-481f-b536-98216f97ef19","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"e668-b496-e264-4283"},{"link_uuid":"ab4b6c5e-285d-4e76-9753-8cb0b6d2fe7b","relation":"blocks","target_id":"e668-b496-e264-4283"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nTwo of the mutation sandbox's protections are asserted against PROXIES rather than against the\nthing that runs in production, so each can be silently unwired without a test failing.\n\n## 1. `sandbox_env` is unbound\n\n`scripts/mutation_sandbox.py:51,223-226` points `HOME` at `/nonexistent-rebar-mutation-home` so\nadjacent home-directory writes fail loudly, and `scripts/mutation_gate.py:597` applies it to both\nshard subprocesses. The runtime behaviour is correct.\n\nThe test is not. `tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py:216-220` asserts on the MAPPING\n`sandbox_env` RETURNS — never on a child process's actual `HOME`. And a repo-wide grep for\n`sandbox_env` across `tests/` matches only `test_mutation_sandbox.py`, so there is no call-site\nbinding test at all. **Deleting `mutation_gate.py:597` leaves the entire suite green.**\n\nThis is the same defect class the author explicitly defended `wrap` against with AST binding\ntests at `test_mutation_sandbox.py:264-301`; `sandbox_env` simply never got the equivalent guard.\n\n## 2. The `mutmut run` deny is tripped against a shape, not against mutmut\n\n`test_enforcement_holds_for_the_mutmut_run_argv_shape` (`:112-122`) trips a real deny, but its\nchild is `sys.executable -c \"import subprocess; subprocess.run(['/bin/sh', ...])\"` — a structural\nproxy for mutmut's process shape. The REAL `mutmut run` call site\n(`scripts/mutation_gate.py:606-615`) is proven wrapped only by AST inspection.\n\n`mutmut run` is the path the original incident took, so this is the one invocation worth proving\nend to end.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A test asserts the CHILD PROCESS's observed `HOME` (not the returned mapping) for both\n      shard subprocesses.\n- [ ] A binding test fails if `sandbox_env` stops being applied at `mutation_gate.py:597`,\n      mirroring the existing AST binding tests for `wrap`.\n- [ ] Mutation-checked: removing the `sandbox_env` call turns at least one test RED.\n- [ ] Either the deny is tripped under a genuine `mutmut run`, or the shape-proxy limitation is\n      recorded explicitly in the test's docstring as a deliberate accepted gap.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["blocks","e668-b496-e264-4283"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["mutation","sandbox","test-integrity"],"ticket_id":"d758-79ab-bb11-4c11","ticket_type":"bug","title":"sandbox_env has no call-site binding test: deleting its only call leaves the suite green","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3d0430a3-9c68-4c11-9a2c-734014af1760","3bee96c3-23b6-481f-b536-98216f97ef19","ab4b6c5e-285d-4e76-9753-8cb0b6d2fe7b"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787865424532978418,"uuid":"f4b99191-85e9-4f50-a5ce-f7f1d2510e4f"}